# M1 / B020 — security-scan, swagger, template-maintenance, verify.

C R197 OL WF-021 | MUST NOT | Security review does not require a specific MCP server, agent, analyzer, commercial scanner or external tool; available tooling is evidence, not the sole authority, and a scanner-reported issue is reported only after inspecting the actual code and its reachability. | security review | none stated
C R198 OL WF-004 | MUST | Verification starts with the final changed-file set and diff: the change matches the requested scope without unrelated refactoring, temporary diagnostics and probes are removed only after preservation, no generated/build artifacts or secrets were added; the final diff is reviewed after all fixes for unrelated edits, commented-out code, temporary logging, unintended TODO/FIXME, stale temporary tests or scripts, architecture drift, unapproved drift from the product sources and stale surfaces after a settings change. | verification | none stated
C R199 OL WF-006 | DEFAULT | For a new runnable application or substantial startup, composition, configuration, persistence or full-stack changes verify the intended Development startup and key composition surfaces (API host starts, endpoint reachable, Swagger UI reachable when expected, configuration binds, database connectivity and initialization, frontend dev server, API base URL and CORS compatibility); a successful build alone does not prove runtime composition. | runtime smoke verification | none stated
C R200 OL RUN-010 | MUST | For every C# file created or modified by the task remove unused or redundant using directives (including those already provided by implicit/global usings unless needed for clarity or disambiguation), verified on the changed files; no unrelated repository-wide using cleanup. | changed C# files | Needed for clarity or disambiguation.
C R201 OL DEP-012 | DECIDED | Swashbuckle Swagger UI is the developer-facing interactive API documentation surface (rather than a standalone raw OpenAPI endpoint); no second competing documentation stack without a concrete need. | API documentation | none stated
C X31 EX WF-020,WF-009 | MUST | The security scan report contains Scope, a Limitations statement (static analysis only), a severity Summary table, Findings and Layer Results for the seven layers with PASS / FINDINGS / NOT APPLICABLE / NOT CHECKED, using the fixed severity scale Critical / High / Medium / Low / Info with defined meanings. | security scan output | none stated | WF-020/WF-009 require contextual severity and truthful status reporting; the oracle does not prescribe report sections, layer tables or a severity scale. | A scan report without the limitations statement or layer results table does not follow the workflow.
C X32 EX - | MUST | Template maintenance procedure: read .claude/MAP.md first; place new content by kind (planning-time governance in the compact CLAUDE.md, stack in technology-stack, capability decisions in docs/capabilities, path rules in flat .claude/rules with paths, procedures in workflow skills, technique in knowledge skills or references, mechanical checks in hooks/scripts wired in settings.json, slot metadata in CONTRACT.md/MODULE.md); keep each policy's trigger role; never hide a must/must-not rule only inside a knowledge skill or private reference; keep the always-loaded surface compact; update MAP.md. | instruction-system maintenance | none stated | Instruction-system maintenance rule; the oracle does not regulate where instruction content lives. | Adding a binding rule only to a knowledge skill violates the maintenance procedure.

